<title>UK: Saudi tells OPEC Aug output at 8.09 mbpd - OPECNA.</title>
<headline>Saudi tells OPEC Aug output at 8.09 mbpd - OPECNA.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saudi Arabia told OPEC it produced 8.09 million barrels per day (bpd) in August but that supply was in line with its 8.0 million bpd quota, the OPEC News Agency (OPECNA) said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Supply, as defined by OPEC, is calculated as domestic consumption, plus net export sales of crude and products, plus withdrawals of stocks held outside national boundaries.</p>
<p>Iran told OPEC it produced 3.593 million bpd, below its quota of 3.6 million, while the United Arab Emirates, Nigeria, Algeria and Qatar said they were producing above quota.</p>
<p>Ten OPEC members have so far submitted production data for August. Data received so far by the secretariat from member countries is as follows (in thousand bpd):  </p>
<p>			Production	   Supply	 OPEC quota</p>
<p> ALGERIA		 772.0		 757.0	  750</p>
<p> INDONESIA	   1,327.6	     1,269.7	1,330</p>
<p> IRAN		  3,593.0	     3,593.0	3,600</p>
<p> IRAQ		    730.0		 730.0	1,200</p>
<p> KUWAIT		2,005.2	     2,005.9	2,000</p>
<p> LIBYA		 1,392.0	     1,399.0	1,390</p>
<p> NIGERIA	     1,866.0	     1,864.9	1,865</p>
<p> QATAR		   396.2		 381.3	  378</p>
<p> SAUDI ARABIA	8,090.0	     8,002.0	8,000</p>
<p> UAE		   2,168.8	     2,166.5	2,161</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7930</p>
